@page "/PluginCacheTagsDemo"
@model LaughTale.Showcase.Pages.PluginCacheTagsDemoModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cache Tags via Plugin API";
}

<div class="app-container" style="max-width: 900px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; padding-bottom: 3rem;">

    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--p-surface-0) 0%, var(--p-surface-50) 100%); border: 1px solid var(--p-border-color); border-radius: 1.25rem; padding: 2.5rem 2rem; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);">
        <h1 style="font-size: 1.875rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--p-text-color); margin: 0;">Cache Tags via Plugin API</h1>
        <p style="color: var(--p-text-muted); font-size: 0.875rem; margin: 0.25rem 0 0;">
            ROADMAP.v5.md Part G/L "Validation: Cache tags" - the same cache + tag + evict story as
            <a href="/CacheTagsDemo">/CacheTagsDemo</a> (Part F), but this page's <code>PageModel</code>
            never calls <code>HttpContext.Tag(...)</code> anywhere. The island below is tagged
            automatically by <code>IslandCacheTagsPlugin</code>, using only the public
            <code>LaughTalePlugin</code> extension points - proof the plugin API alone is expressive
            enough to build real per-island cache invalidation.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div style="background: var(--p-surface-0); border: 1px solid var(--p-border-color); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.75rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
        <div>
            <span class="aura-tag tag-cyan" style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: inline-block;">Rendered at</span>
            <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--p-surface-700); font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700;">@Model.RenderedAtUtc.ToString("HH:mm:ss.fff") UTC</p>
            <p style="margin: 0.25rem 0 0; color: var(--p-text-muted); font-size: 0.75rem;">Nonce: @Model.RenderNonce</p>
        </div>
        <p style="color: var(--p-text-muted); font-size: 0.8125rem; margin: 0;">
            Reload this page repeatedly within 15 seconds - the timestamp and nonce stay IDENTICAL
            (served from cache). Click "Invalidate now" to evict the auto-applied
            <code>island:interactive-counter</code> tag, then reload - the timestamp changes right
            away, exactly as if this page had called <code>HttpContext.Tag(...)</code> by hand.
        </p>
        <a href="/PluginCacheTagsDemoInvalidate" class="p-button p-button-secondary" style="display: inline-block; width: fit-content; text-decoration: none;">Invalidate now</a>
    </div>

    <island name="interactive-counter"
            props="@(new { InitialCount = 0, Step = 1, Label = "Auto-Tagged Counter" })"
            hydrate="Load" />

</div>
